<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_42" targetNamespace="https://kitchen406.local/bpmn">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_42">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_42" name="BPMN-42 | Owner Review Moderation" processRef="Process_42" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_42" name="Owner Review Moderation" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Sources: docs/proposed-bpmn-catalog.md BPMN-42 and related process boundaries; Chapters/Kitchen406 - Capstone Paper.md SRS 4.18 FR-REV-08-14; supporting NFR-SEC-03,08, NFR-REL-03,05. Website: index.html loads app/owner-reviews.js Owner list/detail form, reasons array, submit visibility/version/history handler and R.public, plus app/session-state.js Owner guard. Current BPMN-41 and related catalog BPMNs reviewed for consistency. Scope: Owner views already submitted feedback and chooses unchanged, hide or unhide. BPMN-41 owns submission, rating/photos/purchase eligibility; do not re-run purchase eligibility or resubmit a review here. Authenticated, authorized Admin/Owner page access is an entry precondition handled by BPMN-30 and protected-page routing. No repeated Owner-access decision is modeled in this workflow; server-side authorization remains an underlying requirement (NFR-SEC-03). Hiding requires supported reason (Spam, Abusive language, Off-topic content, Sexual content, Other with specified explanation); unhiding restores visibility without inventing required hiding reason or approval. Record moderator account, action/reason and time in retained history. No automated sentiment analysis, profanity classification, dispute handling or automatic customer notification. Preserve original customer identity/purchase association, rating, comment and photo references; visibility change does not delete/edit feedback content. No external provider exchange is required: all steps are internal Owner/System lanes with sequence flows, no message or signal flows. All local checks and recovery visible. Failed save/stale version preserves saved moderation state and draft, with explicit correct/reload/retry/stop paths. Recovery returns to actual review rather than replaying unrelated initial choices. Same requested visibility already reached creates no duplicate moderation entry; concurrent different state needs refreshed review. Proposed consistent/history safeguards follow SRS reliability beyond in-memory preview. No moderation is implicitly a prepublication approval stage.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_42">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_42_owner" name="Admin/Owner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_42</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
